figuration calls after a voter address change (parsed index 3), an AddNonvoter (index 5) and a RemoveServer (index 7) - while the ConfigurationStore-only control recorded six calls (index 1). The missing callback is therefore not specific to one configuration command, and the command coverage no longer rests on unbound event values.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"c0e1fcddc4fb4abd837447f13492bc56-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":2,\n   \\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The documented StoreConfiguration callback does not arrive for a BatchingFSM, for any of the three configuration commands measured, while the ConfigurationStore-only control receives it.\\\"}],\n \\\"answers\\\":{},\\\"counterevidence\\\":cur['counterevidence'],\\\"limitations\\\":lim,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":cur['joint_history']+\\\" A third revision, 60915351a519403a9c3ee2b96fae7ce2-experiment, re-ran the same four cases with the trigger recorded on the setup event; its cases, counters and control are identical to the previous revision's.\\\"}\nknowledge={\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"c0e1fcddc4fb4abd837447f13492bc56-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":(\\\"An application FSM that implements both BatchingFSM and ConfigurationStore never receives StoreConfiguration for a committed configuration change, even though ConfigurationStore documents that callback as invoked once a configuration change is committed. runFSM decides once whether the FSM implements BatchingFSM and then routes every applied batch through applyBatch; that path sends LogConfiguration entries to ApplyBatch and contains no StoreConfiguration call, while StoreConfiguration is reached only from applySingle, which runs when batching is disabled. Three executions agree: the dual-interface FSM recorded zero StoreConfiguration calls and 5 or 6 ApplyBatch configuration entries after each of three different configuration commands (a voter address change, an AddNonvoter and a RemoveServer), while the ConfigurationStore-only control recorded six calls and no ApplyBatch entries.\\\"),\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"An FSM type whose method set satisfies both interfaces (BatchingFSM embeds FSM, ConfigurationStore embeds FSM); a single committed configuration change produced by AddVoter with a new address, AddNonvoter, or RemoveServer, in a three-voter cluster built with the repository's own helper, in-memory transports and stores.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n \\\"executions\\\":{V1:[1,3], V2:[1,3], V3:[1,3,5,7]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"The premise is unchanged and the evidence is extended: the corrected revision's comparisons resolved for all four cases, so the zero is now established under three different configuration commands rather than one, and the earlier revision's unbound values are superseded by the same values with satisfied comparisons.\\\",\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]}\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpreted the corrected revision. With the setup event carrying the trigger, all four comparisons resolved: the dual-interface FSM recorded zero StoreConfiguration calls after a voter address change, an AddNonvoter and a RemoveServer, while the ConfigurationStore-only control recorded six, so the missing callback is established for three different configuration commands and the earlier revision's unbound values are superseded by the same values with satisfied comparisons. The account now cites all three receipts, its limitations were rewritten accordingly, and the Fact was extended under its own id with the third execution and the command coverage. No earlier receipt is withdrawn and no execution is requested.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[knowledge],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
