{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the corrected revision, which resolved everything the previous one could not: with the setup event carrying the same trigger as the result event, all four comparisons resolved, and each of the three dual-interface cases was contradicted by a valid witness — zero StoreConfiguration calls after a voter address change (index 3), an AddNonvoter (index 5) and a RemoveServer (index 7) — while the ConfigurationStore-only control recorded six calls (index 1). The missing callback is therefore established for three different configuration commands, not one, and the earlier revision's unbound values are superseded by the same values now backed by satisfied comparisons. The account cites all three receipts of this lineage, its limitations were rewritten to say so while keeping the shared-recorder and recovery-consequence caveats, and the Fact was extended under its own id with the third execution and the command list. No earlier receipt was withdrawn and no execution requested. About twenty-five minutes remain; every question now carries an account with receipts, four defects are asserted with reproduced or command-covered witnesses, and two leads are refuted with their counterevidence recorded, so I have no queued measurement left to run.\"}"}}
